    category: "重大事件",
    title: "駭客組織RansomHouse攻擊日本Nichirei，導致大規模冷凍食品供應鏈中斷與個資外洩風險",
    summary: "日本冷鏈龍頭Nichirei集團於7月13日遭駭客攻擊，導致其遍布全國的冷藏配送中心營運中斷，引發食品供應鏈風暴。駭客組織RansomHouse公開聲稱是攻擊者，並在資料外洩網站上將Nichirei列為受害者，威脅公開竊取的敏感資料。此次攻擊嚴重擾亂了Nichirei的物流系統，影響了上千家食品製造商、連鎖超市及餐廳。Nichirei後續公告確認，部分遭未經授權存取的伺服器存在個人資訊，面臨資外洩風險。事件顯示關鍵民生供應鏈極易受網路攻擊影響。Nichirei已發布多波公告，並預計本週內完成系統全面復原，但整體復原耗時預計近兩週。業界應高度關注關鍵基礎設施的網路韌性與供應鏈風險管理。",
    tags: ["Nichirei", "RansomHouse", "供應鏈", "冷凍食品", "資外洩", "關鍵基礎設施"],
    title_en: "Hacker Group RansomHouse Attacks Nichirei, Causing Large-Scale Frozen Food Supply Chain Disruption and Personal Data Leakage Risk",
    summary_en: "Nichirei Group, a leader in Japan's cold chain sector, was attacked by hackers on July 13th, leading to the operational disruption of its refrigerated distribution centers nationwide and triggering a food supply chain crisis. The hacker group RansomHouse publicly claimed responsibility for the attack, listing Nichirei as a victim on a data leak website and threatening to publish stolen sensitive data. This attack severely disrupted Nichirei's logistics system, affecting thousands of food manufacturers, chain supermarkets, and restaurants. Nichirei subsequently announced that some servers accessed without authorization contained personal information, facing a data leakage risk. The incident highlights how vulnerable critical life-sustaining supply chains are to cyberattacks. Nichirei has issued multiple announcements and expects to complete a full system recovery this week, though the overall recovery is estimated to take nearly two weeks. The industry should pay close attention to the cyber resilience and supply chain risk management of critical infrastructure.",
