    summary_en: "Apple has introduced a significant feature upgrade to the 'Photos' application in iOS 27: the 'Save Video Frame as Photo' function. This feature addresses the limitations of previously using screenshots to capture video frames, which often resulted in lower resolution and poor cropping effects. Now, users can simply tap the three-dot icon in the upper right corner while viewing a video to save the currently displayed video frame as a new photo with higher resolution, without needing manual cropping. This allows users to more accurately convert exciting moments from videos into high-quality static photos, greatly enhancing the user experience. Users are advised to upgrade to iOS 27 to utilize this new feature.",
    tags_en: ["iOS 27", "Apple Photos", "Video Capture", "Screenshot", "macOS"],
