    summary_en: "Apple has announced a unique partnership with automotive manufacturer Ford, integrating its Apple Maps mapping service into Ford's upcoming Universal Electric Vehicle (UEV) platform. This integration will be achieved through Apple's new MapKit for Automotive SDK and is expected to be available in 2027. This feature will provide vehicle owners with a more aesthetically pleasing and user-friendly navigation experience, including voice commands, real-time traffic and event information, detailed point-of-interest search, and optimized EV route planning and battery pre-conditioning functions. Furthermore, Ford will utilize Apple Maps' road network data as part of the development of the next-generation BlueCruise hands-free highway driving function, providing a smoother on- and off-ramp experience. While Apple confirmed that CarPlay will remain an option, this direct integration allows Apple Maps to be used even by drivers without an iPhone. This move signals Apple's continued expansion of its ecosystem influence within the in-vehicle entertainment system sector.",
