    summary_en: "At the Galaxy Unpacked event, Samsung, in collaboration with Google, Warby Parker, and Gentle Monster, unveiled the first Android XR smart glasses. The device is expected to feature up to 9 hours of battery life and comes with a charging case. Core functionalities include advanced applications such as real-time voice translation, turn-by-turn navigation, hands-free photo/video capture, and real-time Q&A and voice assistance of the surrounding environment via Google Gemini. Furthermore, the device integrates open-ear audio, allowing users to remain aware of their surroundings while listening to music or podcasts. Notably, the glasses feature a built-in privacy light, which is reportedly capable of detecting if the privacy light is obstructed and subsequently disabling the camera to enhance user privacy. Although the article does not provide specific version numbers or CVE information, it highlights significant advancements in AI integration, multimedia capabilities, and privacy protection, with an expected launch later this year.",
