    title: "歐盟因違反《數位市場法案》對 Google 處以總計 8.9 億歐元的巨額罰款",
    summary: "歐盟宣布對 Google 處以兩筆罰款，總計高達 8.9 億歐元（約 10 億美元），指控其違反《數位市場法案》（DMA）。第一筆 4.6 億歐元的罰款，源於 Google 在 Google 搜尋（Search）中對自身服務給予「偏好待遇」，導致其購物、飯店、交通等結果比第三方服務更顯眼。第二筆 4.3 億歐元的罰款，則針對 Google 限制開發者在 Google Play Store 以外的渠道進行「自由溝通、推廣優惠及簽訂合約」，違反了開發者選擇權的原則。歐盟要求 Google 在 60 天內支付罰款，否則將根據其全球營收處以額外罰款。Google 雖已提出修改方案，但歐盟仍持續評估其合規性，並指出這屬於歐盟對 Google「守門人」（gatekeeping）行為的持續監管。",
    tags: ["Google", "歐盟", "Digital Markets Act", "DMA", "Google Search", "Google Play Store", "反壟斷"],
    title_en: "EU Imposes Total Fine of €890 Million on Google for Violating Digital Markets Act",
    summary_en: "The EU announced two separate fines against Google, totaling €890 million (approximately $1 billion), for alleged violations of the Digital Markets Act (DMA). The first fine, amounting to €460 million, stems from Google giving its own services 'preferential treatment' within Google Search, making its own shopping, hotel, and travel results more prominent than those of third-party services. The second fine, totaling €430 million, targets Google's restriction on developers' ability to 'freely communicate, promote offers, and sign contracts' outside of the Google Play Store, violating the principle of developer choice. The EU has required Google to pay the fines within 60 days, or face additional penalties based on its global revenue. Although Google has proposed modifications, the EU continues to assess its compliance, noting that this represents ongoing EU oversight of Google's 'gatekeeping' practices.",
    tags_en: ["Google", "EU", "Digital Markets Act", "DMA", "Google Search", "Google Play Store", "Antitrust"],
    sources: [
      { name: "9to5Google", url: "https://9to5google.com/2026/07/23/european-union-fines-google-in-antitrust-for-search-play-store", lang: "EN" }
    ]
