    title_en: "Google Home Launches Gemini Voice Assistant Update and Nest Cam Firmware Upgrade, Enhancing Smart Home Interaction and Connectivity Stability",
    summary_en: "Google recently released multiple updates across its smart home ecosystem. Regarding voice assistants, Gemini for Home and the mobile application have updated the conversational memory feature, expanding the context window to 15 minutes, allowing users to engage in more natural follow-up questions. Furthermore, the Gemini Live feature has been expanded to multiple Google Home devices, offering a deeper conversational experience. The Google Home application (Android/iOS) version 4.22 also brings optimized automation settings and enhances security by adding a reminder to manually change the password when removing a member from the smart lock function. For the Nest Cam series, Google also released a firmware update scheduled for July 2026. This update aims to improve device connectivity reliability, optimize the setup process for new devices, and fix issues related to activity zone detection and application stability. The practical impact of these updates is providing users with a more cohesive and secure smart home experience. Users are advised to pay attention to and install the latest applications and device firmware.",
