    title: "Google 推出「自拍影片」登入驗證機制，強化帳號防盜與多層次安全保護",
    summary: "Google 為增強帳號安全性，推出新的「自拍影片」（selfie video）登入驗證方式。此功能旨在解決用戶在遺失手機或無法使用密碼金鑰（passkeys）時，仍能安全登入 Google 帳號的問題。用戶需透過設備的相機，完成一系列短暫的、指導式的頭部動作，以捕捉多個角度的影片。該機制強調多層次安全，能有效防止使用偽造照片或影片（deepfakes）進行冒用。當用戶無法使用常規設備時，只需再次拍攝自拍影片進行驗證。Google 表示，該影片資料會加密儲存，且預設僅用於登入驗證。用戶可隨時刪除此影片，並可選擇是否允許資料用於改善驗證方法。Google 建議用戶結合此方法與密碼金鑰、恢復聯絡人等多種驗證方式，以建立更完整的安全防線。",
    tags: ["Google 帳號", "自拍影片", "多因素驗證", "Passkeys", "資安強化", "Deepfake 防護"],
    title_en: "Google introduces 'selfie video' login verification mechanism to enhance account theft protection and multi-layered security",
    summary_en: "To enhance account security, Google has introduced a new 'selfie video' login verification method. This feature aims to solve the problem of users still being able to securely log into their Google account even if they lose their phone or cannot use passkeys. Users must use the device's camera to complete a series of short, guided head movements, capturing videos from multiple angles. This mechanism emphasizes multi-layered security and can effectively prevent impersonation using fake photos or videos (deepfakes). When users cannot use their regular device, they simply need to record a selfie video for verification. Google states that this video data will be encrypted and is initially used only for login verification. Users can delete this video at any time and can choose whether to allow the data to be used for improving verification methods. Google recommends that users combine this method with multiple verification methods, such as passkeys and recovery contacts, to establish a more comprehensive security defense line.",
    tags_en: ["Google Account", "Selfie Video", "Multi-Factor Authentication", "Passkeys", "Cybersecurity Enhancement", "Deepfake Protection"],
    sources: [
      { name: "9to5Google", url: "https://9to5google.com/2026/07/23/google-account-selfie-video", lang: "EN" }
    ]
