    title_en: "Apple TV announces documentary series 'The Last Person on Earth,' focusing on relationship and emotional exploration",
    summary_en: "This article introduces a documentary series announced by Apple TV titled 'The Last Person on Earth.' The series features renowned relationship therapist and New York Times bestselling author Esther Perel, aiming to explore human relationships and emotional connection. Although labeled a 'documentary series,' its content description and concept (pairing seemingly opposing couples and taking them to romantic, remote locations) bear a strong resemblance to reality television. Perel noted that while love craves intimacy, desire stems from 'otherness,' encouraging people to break free from established relationship patterns and view dating as a process of exploring unknown adventures. The series is scheduled to premiere around 2027. Furthermore, Apple recently announced an adaptation of a bestselling novel, indicating that Apple TV is actively expanding its content types, venturing into the romance genre in addition to its existing sci-fi, comedy, and thriller genres. Apple TV's current subscription fee is $12.99 per month, or can be discounted through the Apple One bundle.",
