    summary_en: "This article reveals the extreme risks associated with using AI chatbots for medical consultation. It points out that ChatGPT once advised a pastor to ignore symptoms of pulmonary embolism. Pulmonary embolism is a fatal disease with a mortality rate as high as 30%. AI's erroneous advice could potentially lead to the worsening of conditions and even trigger legal lawsuits. This serves as a reminder that although AI chatbots are powerful, they absolutely cannot replace professional medical diagnosis. Users should treat information provided by AI as merely reference material and must seek diagnosis and advice from qualified medical professionals.",
