    title_en: "AMD Unveils Instinct MI455X Accelerator and Helios AI Rack, Featuring 2nm Process and HBM4 Memory",
    summary_en: "At AI 2026, AMD unveiled the new Instinct MI455X GPU accelerator and introduced the Helios AI rack, which integrates the MI455X, AMD EPYC Venice CPU, and AMD Pensando networking. The MI455X utilizes a 2nm process and is equipped with 432GB HBM4 memory. Its peak MXFP8 and MXFP4 performance reaches four times that of the Instinct MI355X, representing a significant generational upgrade. The higher HBM capacity of the MI455X also enhances support for large AI models. The Helios platform is currently in full production and is expected to begin shipping by the end of this quarter, with gradually increasing shipment volumes in Q4 2027 and H1 2027. Each Helios rack provides 4,600 CPU cores and 18,000 GPU compute units. AMD also confirmed that the Instinct MI500 series will launch in 2027, and the Instinct MI600 series will launch in 2028.",
    tags_en: ["AMD", "Instinct MI455X", "Helios", "AI Accelerator", "HBM4", "2nm", "AI Computing"],
